The goal isn’t ambiguity for its own sake. It’s constructive polysemy—multiple readings that reinforce the same underlying operator rather than competing with each other.

In that sense, a good pun isn’t merely a joke. It’s a small demonstration that one representation can faithfully carry several compatible structures at once.